# Daily verified snapshot of the LIVE database.
#
# The live database is inside the Coolify volume
# rboj5u2xk5dj4o4yto89ablh_patente-data, not on the host filesystem. This job used
# to point at /srv/patente/patente.db — the old systemd deployment — which meant the
# real data (progress, entitlement, and the explanations and translations that cost
# money to generate) was being left unprotected while a backup ran successfully
# every night against the wrong database. That is the worst shape a backup can take.
#
# /usr/local/sbin/patente-backup snapshots inside the container using SQLite's
# online backup API, rehearses a restore against it, and only then copies it out.
# It exits non-zero on any failure, so cron will report it.
#
# Runs as root because it needs the Docker socket.
#
# NOTE: /var/backups is ON THIS BOX. This is still not the off-box copy that
# STATUS.md §6.4 asks for.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
MAILTO=root

# Every 6 hours. Daily meant losing up to a day of progress, entitlement and paid-for
# generated content; 6-hourly with 56 retained keeps 14 days of history at the same
# disk cost as the old 14 daily snapshots (each is ~2.7 MB and mostly the static bank).
# This is an interim tightening - the full scheme (off-box, tiered retention) is next.
0 */6 * * * root /usr/local/sbin/patente-backup >> /var/log/patente-backup.log 2>&1
